.TH hs-relmon 1 2026-09-10 "sandogasa 0.24.0" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
hs\-relmon \- Release monitoring tool for CentOS Hyperscale SIG packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhs\-relmon\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Release monitoring tool for CentOS Hyperscale SIG packages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS hs-relmon check-latest
\fBhs\-relmon check\-latest\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-distros\fR] [\fB\-\-repology\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-track\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-file\-issue\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.PP
Check the latest version of a package across distributions
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-distros\fR \fI<DISTROS>\fR
Comma\-separated list of distros to check.

Valid names:
  upstream         Newest version across all repos
  fedora           Fedora Rawhide + latest stable
  fedora\-rawhide   Fedora Rawhide only
  fedora\-stable    Latest stable Fedora only
  centos           Latest CentOS Stream
  centos\-stream    Latest CentOS Stream
  hyperscale / hs  Hyperscale EL9 + EL10
  hs9              Hyperscale EL9 only
  hs10             Hyperscale EL10 only
.TP
\fB\-\-repology\-name\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Override Repology project name when it differs
from the package (e.g. linux for perf).
.TP
\fB\-\-track\fR \fI<TRACK>\fR [default: upstream]
Distribution to compare Hyperscale builds against.

Valid names:
  upstream         Newest version across all repos (default)
  fedora\-rawhide   Fedora Rawhide
  fedora\-stable    Latest stable Fedora
  centos           Latest CentOS Stream
  centos\-stream    Latest CentOS Stream
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-\-file\-issue\fR [\fI<URL>\fR]
File or update a GitLab issue if the package is
outdated. Searches for an open issue labeled
rfe::new\-version and updates its title, or creates
a new one. Defaults to
https://gitlab.com/CentOS/Hyperscale/rpms/PKG.
Uses the token from \*(Aqhs\-relmon config\*(Aq, or
GITLAB_TOKEN env var as an override.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
Source package name (e.g. ethtool)
.SS hs-relmon check-manifest
\fBhs\-relmon check\-manifest\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMANIFEST\fR> 
.PP
Check all packages listed in a manifest file
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of tables
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-status\fR \fI<STATUS>\fR
Only show packages whose GitLab issue matches this
work\-item status. Packages without an issue are
excluded. Issues that do not match are not updated.

Default statuses:
  To do          Planned but not started
  In progress    Currently being worked on
  Done           Completed
  Canceled       Will not be done
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-assignee\fR \fI<USERNAME>\fR
Only show packages whose GitLab issue is assigned
to this username. Use "none" to match unassigned
issues. Packages without an issue or without a
matching assignee are excluded.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIMANIFEST\fR>
Path to the TOML manifest file
.SS hs-relmon dupe-subpkgs
\fBhs\-relmon dupe\-subpkgs\fR [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-fix\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Find binary RPMs shipped by 2+ source packages in a tag
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories to scan.
The repository is the segment between `\-packages\-`
and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-release`. Each
repository\*(Aqs `\-release` and `\-testing` tags across
EL9/EL10 (and the Stream variants) are scanned.
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR
Hyperscale release(s) to scan, repeatable or comma\-
separated. Each value is a short EL token (`9`, `9s`,
`10`, `10s`) or the equivalent full release name
(`hyperscale9s`, `hyperscale10s`, ...) — both forms
mean the same release. Defaults to all four.
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Source package name(s), repeatable or comma\-separated.
Only collisions that involve one of these sources are
reported (the whole tag is still scanned to find what
they collide with). Defaults to all packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-fix\fR
For each collision, show the candidate builds and the
binaries only each one provides (which would vanish
from the tag if it were untagged), then prompt for
which build to untag. Defaults to skipping. Requires
CBS write authentication. In \-\-json mode or without a
terminal the plan is printed and nothing is untagged.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS hs-relmon file-conflicts
\fBhs\-relmon file\-conflicts\fR [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Find files shipped by 2+ sources across enabled repos
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR
Comma\-separated repositories that are enabled together
on a host, compared per EL version. Overrides the
per\-EL defaults (main + kernel on EL10/10s; main only
on EL9/9s, which has no kernel repo). The `\-release`
tag of each is combined and files owned by two or more
distinct source packages are flagged.
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR
Hyperscale release(s) to scan, repeatable or comma\-
separated. Each value is a short EL token (`9`, `9s`,
`10`, `10s`) or the equivalent full release name
(`hyperscale9s`, `hyperscale10s`, ...) — both forms
mean the same release. Defaults to all four.
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Source package name(s), repeatable or comma\-separated.
Only conflicts that involve one of these sources are
reported (the whole repo set is still scanned to find
what they conflict with). Defaults to all packages.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS hs-relmon list-issues
\fBhs\-relmon list\-issues\fR [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-issue\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-manifest\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-missing\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
List GitLab issues labeled rfe::new\-version
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR [default: https://gitlab.com/CentOS/Hyperscale/rpms]
GitLab group URL to search
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-status\fR \fI<STATUS>\fR
Only show issues matching this work\-item status.

Default statuses:
  To do          Planned but not started
  In progress    Currently being worked on
  Done           Completed
  Canceled       Will not be done
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-assignee\fR \fI<USERNAME>\fR
Only show issues assigned to this username.
Use "none" to match unassigned issues.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of a table
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a TOML manifest file. When provided, the
output shows which packages with rfe::new\-version
issues are missing from the manifest.
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-missing\fR
Add packages that have rfe::new\-version issues but
are missing from the manifest. Requires \-\-manifest.
Packages are inserted in sorted order.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS hs-relmon prune-archived
\fBhs\-relmon prune\-archived\fR [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMANIFEST\fR> 
.PP
Untag CBS builds for archived\-upstream packages stock caught up to
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories to manage.
The repository is the segment between `\-packages\-`
and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-release`. Tags whose
repository is not in this list are not touched.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated packages to skip
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview operations without applying them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Untag at/behind\-stock without prompting; skip ahead\-of\-stock
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIMANIFEST\fR>
Path to the TOML manifest file
.SS hs-relmon prune-manifest
\fBhs\-relmon prune\-manifest\fR [\fB\-\-release\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-testing\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMANIFEST\fR> 
.PP
Untag old hyperscale builds for every package in a manifest, keeping N newest in each `\-release`/`\-testing` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-release\-keep\fR \fI<RELEASE_KEEP>\fR [default: 2]
Builds to keep per `\-release` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-testing\-keep\fR \fI<TESTING_KEEP>\fR [default: 1]
Builds to keep per `\-testing` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories to manage.
The repository is the segment between `\-packages\-`
and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-release`. Tags whose
repository is not in this list are not touched.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated package names to skip during the
batch run. Useful when one package manages its own
tag cleanup (e.g. systemd) and you don\*(Aqt want this
tool to touch it.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview operations without applying them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the per\-package confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIMANIFEST\fR>
Path to the TOML manifest file
.SS hs-relmon prune-tags
\fBhs\-relmon prune\-tags\fR [\fB\-\-release\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-testing\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.PP
Untag old hyperscale builds for one package, keeping N newest in each `\-release`/`\-testing` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-release\-keep\fR \fI<RELEASE_KEEP>\fR [default: 2]
Builds to keep per `\-release` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-testing\-keep\fR \fI<TESTING_KEEP>\fR [default: 1]
Builds to keep per `\-testing` tag
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories to manage.
The repository is the segment between `\-packages\-`
and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-release`. Tags whose
repository is not in this list are not touched.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview operations without applying them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
Source package name (e.g. ethtool)
.SS hs-relmon check-repos
\fBhs\-relmon check\-repos\fR [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-gitlab\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMANIFEST\fR> 
.PP
Interactively review builds in hyperscale `\-testing` tags and promote (+1), reject (\-1), or skip (0) each one. Compare every manifest package\*(Aqs Hyperscale builds against stock: still ahead, or caught up — and then whether to retire it or rebase it, per the manifest\*(Aqs `divergent`. Check every manifest package\*(Aqs GitLab repo against the SIG\*(Aqs conventions — default branch the newest Hyperscale branch, merge requests fast\-forwarded — and set them with `\-\-apply`
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated packages to check (default: all)
.TP
\fB\-\-gitlab\-group\fR \fI<URL>\fR [default: https://gitlab.com/CentOS/Hyperscale/rpms]
GitLab group the packages\*(Aq repos live under
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Set what differs, asking per repo (`a` for the rest, `q` to stop)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Apply to every repo without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIMANIFEST\fR>
Path to the TOML manifest file
.SS hs-relmon check-stock
\fBhs\-relmon check\-stock\fR [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMANIFEST\fR> 
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories whose
`\-release`/`\-testing` tags are compared against
stock. The repository is the segment between
`\-packages\-` and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-release`.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated packages to skip
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR[=\fI<WHEN>\fR] [default: auto]
Colorize the verdicts, as `ls \-\-color`: `\-\-color` alone is `always`; `auto` (the default) colors a TTY unless NO_COLOR is set; `never`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Auto\-detect: enable on a TTY when `NO_COLOR` is unset
.IP \(bu 2
always: Force colored output even when piped
.IP \(bu 2
never: Disable colored output entirely
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIMANIFEST\fR>
Path to the TOML manifest file
.SS hs-relmon retire
\fBhs\-relmon retire\fR [\fB\-\-gitlab\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-manifest\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.PP
Retire package(s) stock now carries: untag their builds from every hyperscale tag, drop them from the manifest, archive their GitLab repos
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to the TOML manifest file to drop them from
.TP
\fB\-\-gitlab\-group\fR \fI<URL>\fR [default: https://gitlab.com/CentOS/Hyperscale/rpms]
GitLab group the packages\*(Aq repos live under
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the plan without untagging, editing or archiving
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Retire a package the manifest declares `divergent` (carrying SIG changes), which is otherwise refused
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Retire without confirming; never untags a build newer than stock, and then leaves the package in place
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
Package(s) to retire
.SS hs-relmon review
\fBhs\-relmon review\fR [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\fR] [\fB\-\-changelog\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fITARGET\fR] 
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<REPOSITORIES>\fR [default: main]
Comma\-separated Hyperscale repositories to scan.
The repository is the segment between `\-packages\-`
and the stage suffix, e.g. `main` in
`hyperscale10s\-packages\-main\-testing`.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR \fI<SKIP>\fR
Package name(s) to exclude from review, repeatable
or comma\-separated. Use for packages with their own
release pipeline (e.g. systemd) that should never be
promoted through this tool.
.TP
\fB\-\-changelog\-lines\fR \fI<CHANGELOG_LINES>\fR [default: 20]
For a package with nothing yet in release, show at
most this many lines of its changelog (a new package
has no prior version to diff against). Packages that
are already in release always show just the entries
newer than the released build.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
List the builds that would be reviewed, then exit
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fITARGET\fR]
Optional package name or build NVR. With a package name, reviews its latest build in each testing tag; with an NVR, reviews that specific build; omitted, reviews everything in testing
.SS hs-relmon config
\fBhs\-relmon config\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Configure GitLab authentication
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
